# Docs — working directories (plans, PRDs, tasks, reports, reviews,
# archive, and other in-progress notes) stay ignored, but the governance
# subtree is versioned: the canonical architecture contract, ADRs, and
# policy/migration/security docs must be reviewable on GitHub and present
# in fresh clones, because tracked entry-point docs (README, CONTRIBUTING,
# AGENTS) link into them. The leading `/` anchors to the repo-root `docs/`
# only, so `apps/docs/content/docs/` — the Fumadocs content collection —
# is unaffected and stays tracked.
/docs/*
!/docs/architecture/
!/docs/adr/
!/docs/policies/
!/docs/migration/
!/docs/security/

.idea/
.gstack/
patches/
.claude/state/
# inline-style→tailwind codemod backups
.codemod-backups/
